────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WEB SOURCE NATURE (faithful-parity note)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
`components/forms/VehicleMultiSelect.tsx` is a CONTROLLED popover multi-select. Its real hooks are
`useTranslation` + `useId`; the fleet arrives as the `vehicles: Vehicle[]` PROP (the parent Alert Studio
editor owns `useVehicles()`), and every edit routes out through the `onChange` prop. The prompt's data-source
list ("useVehicles, useTranslation, useId") is the domain extraction; the component itself never fetches.
Mirroring the accepted sibling VehicleSelect (0164), the native peer reconciles the prop-driven web with the
P4 "every state renders" contract via a P1/S8 Source→Snapshot→Model seam: the host implements the source over
its `useVehicles()` feed + the editor's controlled value, and the surface adds the always-render leaf states
(loading skeleton, fetch-error retry) + the freshness chip ON TOP of the faithful web body. No HTTP in the
view. No web branch invented away; no fetch chrome fabricated beyond the P4 leaf contract.

